.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\n- \"At harvesting, maize grains are usually not fully dry and have a moisture content of about 15 to 20%. Immediately after harvesting, cobs should be dried so as to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% in readiness for storage.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]\n- \"Maize should be stored after removal of maize husks and shelling. Storing unhusked maize is not recommended as it is very difficult to detect insect infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible pest/disease: this is not a diagnosis. Officer should inspect or refer.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1444, "completion_tokens": 268}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1332, "completion_tokens": 160}}, "cost_usd": 0.000346}}
{"task": "F7", "q": "Some of my stored maize is mouldy. Can I sell it or feed it to animals?", "auto": "pass", "auto_problems": [], "status": "pending_review", "priority": "urgent", "clarification": "", "urgent_reasons": ["food safety terms in question", "citation check failed: 'The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration set lower limits a…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Incorrect EU limit; 'Do not confirm whether the maize exceeds these limits.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage does not"], "sources": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying", "AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "source_checks": [["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE", true], ["AGBETIAMEH-2018", true]], "errors": [], "draft_mode": "stub(citation-check-fallback after llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct)", "language": "en", "citation_check": {"ok": false, "attempts": [{"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No warning", "'Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which are harmful to humans and animals.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Only limits", "'If the maize is mouldy, it is likely to exceed this limit.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: No link"], "figures_checked": 1, "sentences_checked": 5, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Do not sell or feed the mouldy maize.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No warning"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which are harmful to humans and animals.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Only limits"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "The Ghana Standards Authority has set a limit of 15 ppb for aflatoxins in maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches limit"}, {"n": 4, "sentence": "If the maize is mouldy, it is likely to exceed this limit.", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "No link"}, {"n": 5, "sentence": "It is important to ensure that maize is properly dried, shelled, and treated with recommended storage chemicals before storage [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling][APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks][APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying].", "cited": ["APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks", "APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches advice"}]}}, {"draft_mode": "llm:mistralai/mistral-small-3.2-24b-instruct", "ok": false, "problems": ["'The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration set lower limits a…' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Incorrect EU limit", "'Do not confirm whether the maize exceeds these limits.' is not supported by its citation according to the judge model: Passage does not"], "figures_checked": 3, "sentences_checked": 3, "judge": {"model": "meta-llama/llama-3.3-70b-instruct", "verdicts": [{"n": 1, "sentence": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which are regulated by the Ghana Standards Authority at a limit of 15 ppb for maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "supported", "why": "Matches passage"}, {"n": 2, "sentence": "The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration set lower limits at 4 ppb and 20 ppb, respectively [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits].", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Incorrect EU limit"}, {"n": 3, "sentence": "Do not confirm whether the maize exceeds these limits.", "cited": ["AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits"], "verdict": "not_supported", "why": "Passage does not"}]}}], "rejected_draft": "Mouldy maize may contain aflatoxins, which are regulated by the Ghana Standards Authority at a limit of 15 ppb for maize [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The European Union and the United States Food and Drugs Administration set lower limits at 4 ppb and 20 ppb, respectively [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]. The officer should choose which limit to follow. Do not confirm whether the maize exceeds these limits."}, "draft": "[OFFLINE STUB DRAFT - no language model was used; text is assembled from retrieved passages]\nWhat the curated sources say:\n- \"Maize should be stored after removal of maize husks and shelling. Storing unhusked maize is not recommended as it is very difficult to detect insect infestations.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-shelling]\n- \"Well dried and shelled maize should be treated with recommended storage chemicals and stored in jute sacks lined with polythene bags.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-sacks]\n- \"At harvesting, maize grains are usually not fully dry and have a moisture content of about 15 to 20%. Immediately after harvesting, cobs should be dried so as to reduce the grain moisture content to about 10 to 12% in readiness for storage.\" [APNI-SARI-2023-MAIZE:p22-drying]\n- \"aflatoxin limits imposed by the European Union (4 ppb), the Ghana Standards Authority (GSA; 15 ppb for maize and 20 ppb for groundnut), and the United States Food and Drugs Administration (FDA; 20 ppb)\" [AGBETIAMEH-2018:aflatoxin-limits]\nNote: Chemical use: AgriReach does not recommend products or doses. Refer to the label and the officer.\nNote: Possible food-safety risk (mould/aflatoxin): AgriReach cannot clear produce for sale, food or feed. Officer should advise.\nNote: The model draft failed the citation check, so the verbatim passages are shown instead.", "drafted_by": "stub", "usage": {"attempted": 4, "calls": 4, "failed": 0, "errors": [], "by_role": {"draft": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1681, "completion_tokens": 280}, "judge": {"calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 1672, "completion_tokens": 184}}, "cost_usd": 0.000609}}
